    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0964" n="750" xml:id="pg750"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 348.</seg></opener>
                <head>General Sickles to Mr.
                        Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 236.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Madrid,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 27, 1870</date>. (Received January 28,
                        1871.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The following is the text of a telegram,
                    sent partly in cipher, from this legation yesterday:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton Fish</hi>, [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Recommandée.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>May I propose, as a modification of Spanish bases, that arbitrators shall bear
                    all claims hot before adjudged by a competent tribunal conformably to seventh
                    article of treaty of ninety-five? Duplicate answer by French cable.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">SICKLES.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">December</hi>
                    26.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. E. SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
